@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@*
    The site's sitewide footer (apps/site/src/components/Footer.astro), rebuilt here
    because Astro and Blazor share no rendering system to render one component from —
    the two are kept in sync by hand, the same way `site.ts`'s `legal.entity` and this
    file's "REEFACT" already have to be (see the KNOWN DUPLICATION note on `site.legal`).

    Root-relative links only (`/about/`, `/privacy/`), never relative: `wwwroot/index.html`
    sets `<base href="/playground/" />`, so a relative "about" would resolve to
    `/playground/about` — a page that does not exist — while a leading-slash path ignores
    that base and correctly reaches the Astro site, which is served from the same
    artefact, at the same root (§12.2). `Pages/NotFound.razor`'s own "go back to the
    site" link already relies on the same rule.

    MainLayout only, not BareLayout: BareLayout renders `/hero`, the widget embedded in
    the landing page's own hero, which is chromeless by design — it already sits inside
    a page that carries the real footer around it, so a second one here would be a
    duplicate, not a consistency.
*@

<main class="page">
    @Body
</main>

<footer class="site-footer">
    <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="/about/">About</a>
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/Reefact/justdummies.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Source code
            <span class="visually-hidden"> opens in a new tab</span>
        </a>
    </nav>
    <p class="copyright">© @DateTime.Now.Year REEFACT</p>
</footer>
